# bash-Folder-organiser

Bash-folder-organiser built to structure files into different categories and putting them in their folders.

## Problem_Statement​

Look at your Downloads folder. Photos, PDFs, installers, ZIP files, CVs, all mixed together. Your mission: build organise.sh, a tool that tidies any folder in seconds by sorting files into sub-folders by type.

## 📌 Project Goals​

- Automated File Categorization

- Non-Destructive Execution

- On-Demand Folder Creation

- Data Loss Prevention

- Fault Tolerance & Resilience

- User Feedback & Logging

## Tech stack

- Bash
- ShellCheck
- Git & Github

## screenshot

![bash script] ![alt text](<asset/image/Screenshot From 2026-11-01 17-36-43.png>)

## Features

- Case-Insensitive File Matching

- Non-Recursive Processing

- On-Demand Folder Creation

- Collision Protection (No Overwriting) 

- Self-Exclusion

- Execution Logging & Summary

## installation and setup

clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/abigailbekwah/bash-Folder-organiser.git
- chmod +x organiser.sh
- ./organiser.sh
```

